  "description": "A center-hall Colonial in Fox Hollow with 2,686 square feet across three levels and five bedrooms. The room that sets it apart is the 20 x 17 conservatory at the back of the house: cathedral ceilings, built-in cabinetry, recessed lighting, window seats, and a wall of windows that opens onto the patio. The rest of the main level holds a formal living room and dining room, a large eat-in kitchen with upgraded counters and stainless appliances, a family room off the kitchen with a wood-burning fireplace, main-floor laundry, and a fifth bedroom with a full bathroom alongside it that works as a guest room or a home office. Four more bedrooms are upstairs, including an ensuite primary, served by two additional full baths. The basement is fully finished and adds usable space below grade. Outside, a stamped concrete front porch and a brick patio with a slate extension look out over a large flat yard with mature landscaping and a brick-outlined walkway. Hardwood runs through much of the home, and there is a two-car attached garage with inside access plus four driveway spaces. The roof is approximately five years old and the hot water heater approximately three. Convenient to Routes 70 and 73, I-295 and the New Jersey Turnpike.",
